  "scope": "Full24 optional-C-write private prototype parity and captured execution timing.\n\nSame original checkpoint/all24/E32/top8/H1024/I512 and original baseline/gates.\nActual MXFP8 tensor-core native D is consumed. Explicit experimental kernel\nrounds C, SiLU and product to BF16 before SFD normalization. Frozen independent\noracle recasts reconstructed logical operands to BF16, applies stock BF16 dot,\nand BF16 SiLU/product. This declared numerical recipe is fixed before tests;\nit is not a replacement for failed native execution. K32 native dot order is retained; the only new execution configuration is\nOmit intermediate C stores, versus emit C stores. C output is explicitly\nunavailable in the private omit mode; its workspace is still allocated by\nthe unmodified wrapper. This is not a public wrapper/API contract change.\nThis can save write traffic but does not save allocation or shared memory.\nBoth modes explicitly acquire D store pipeline after commit, before SMEM reuse.\nPrior failed loader and no-C/D-TMA-reuse evidence is preserved separately. The independent oracle is unchanged. No native BF16\nmatrix multiplication, fallback, support bypass or production edit.\n",
